s://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T11:18:38Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T11:18:38Z","body":"> @groud Note the distinction between CanvasItem::is_set_as_top_level() and Control::is_top_level_control().\r\n\r\nAh right, I edited my message consequently.\r\n\r\n> The latter is only used in one place in Control::get_root_parent_control(), which is itself only used in one place Viewport::_gui_set_drag_preview. These are internal functions, not exposed.\r\n\r\nAh right, I assumed this was used more and exposed. Though, even if internal, they are not editor-only function and such change could break drag-&-drop.\r\n\r\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101745\r\n\r\nAh that's some good context. \r\n\r\nAlright I guess it can work, but we should be quite wary about such change. I still am not sure this does not break anything. I guess we can try it out though, if we don't find a situation where it breaks drag&drop we should be fine.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789344176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789385438","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105167#issuecomment-2789385438","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105167","id":2789385438,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mQqTe","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T11:35:59Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T11:35:59Z","body":"Superseded by #101745. Thanks for the contribution!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789385438/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790447755","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105167#issuecomment-2790447755","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105167","id":2790447755,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mUtqL","user":{"login":"mdkdir","id":42262007,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjYyMDA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42262007?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir","html_url":"https://github.com/mdkdir","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdkdir/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T17:23:25Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T17:23:25Z","body":"> This does not optimize the function, it seems to completely change its behavior instead. `is_set_as_top_level` is a property, and it's now completely removed from the code. See there: https://docs.godotengine.org/de/4.x/classes/class_canvasitem.html#class-canvasitem-property-top-level\r\n> \r\n> I would refrain doing that kind of change without an issue associated with it anyway. We can't risk breaking compatibility for optimizations.\r\n\r\nApologies, I never intended to break compatibility. It was an error on my part to use `parent_control` instead of `parent_canvas_item`. I looked it over many times but didn't notice this mistake. I have pushed a [corrected version](https://github.com/mason1920/godot/commit/4a288905d4713be595d3938ffccec785e88df1e9). At this point it would just be a minor optimization, avoiding the calls to get_parent_item(). I find the solution in #101745 satisfactory, so I would understand if a pull request is not justified for such a minor change.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790447755/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]